<title>USA: Olin Corp Q1 shr $0.80 vs $0.85.</title>
<headline>Olin Corp Q1 shr $0.80 vs $0.85.</headline>
<dateline>NORWALK, Conn. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>OLIN CORPORATION</p>
<p>		     Consolidated Statements of Income, UNAUDITED</p>
<p>		    (In millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>							     Three Months</p>
<p>							   Ended March 31,</p>
<p>								1997  1996(A)</p>
<p> Sales							$591.2 $692.9</p>
<p> Income from Continuing Operations		    41.8   50.7</p>
<p>    Loss from Disc. Operations, Net of Taxes(B)     --  (5.7)</p>
<p> Net Income						   41.8   45.0</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss) Per Common Share:</p>
<p>Primary:</p>
<p>    Continuing operations				 0.81   0.99</p>
<p>    Discontinued Operations				--  (0.12)</p>
<p> Total Net Income					   0.81   0.87</p>
<p>Fully Diluted:</p>
<p>    Continuing operations				 0.80   0.96</p>
<p>    Discontinued Operations				--  (0.11)</p>
<p> Total Net Income					   0.80   0.85</p>
<p> Average Common Shrs Outstanding - Primary	  51.9   49.6</p>
<p> Average Common Shrs Outstanding - Fully Diluted  52.2   51.9</p>
<p>NOTE: (A)  The three months ended March 31, 1996 operating results include the isocyanates businesses which were sold on December 4, 1996 (sales $81.5 million, operating income $19.5 million, fully diluted earnings per share $0.26)</p>
<p>(B)  Represents the net losses of the former Aerospace and Ordnance divisions spun-off as Primex Technologies Inc on December 31, 1996.</p>
